  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef and Paja are bored, so they are playing an infinite game of ping pong. The rules of the game are as follows:\n\n\nThe players play an infinite number of games. At the end of each game, the player who won it scores a point.\nIn each game, one of the players serves. Chef serves in the first game.\nAfter every KKK points are scored (regardless of which players scored them), i.e. whenever KKK games have been played since the last time the serving player changed, the player that serves in the subsequent games changes: if Chef served in the game that just finished, then Paja will serve in the next game and all subsequent games until the serving player changes again; if Paja served, then Chef will serve.\nThe players got a little too caught up in the game and they forgot who is supposed to serve in the next game. Will you help them determine that? So far, Chef has scored XXX points and Paja has scored YYY points.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\le T \\le 501≤T≤50",
      "0≤X,Y≤1090 \\le X, Y \\le 10^90≤X,Y≤109",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\le K \\le 10^91≤K≤109",
      "Subtasks"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains three space-separated integers XXX, YYY and KKK.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing the string `\"Chef\"` if Chef is supposed to serve next or `\"Paja\"` otherwise (without quotes).",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1 3 3\n5 7 2\n38657 76322 564",
        "output": "Paja\nChef\nPaja",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: Chef served for the first three games, after that Paja started serving. He only served in one game, so he is supposed to serve next."
      }
    ]
  },
